 "payload": {
  "question": "By when must we implement a mitigation plan created under CIP-007-6 R2 Part 2.3? Does the standard set an outer deadline, and does our procedure?",
  "ref": "CIP-007-6 R2 Part 2.4",
  "answer": "## The standard's answer\n\nPart 2.4's duty text (csection-c0cd08b61c308b0e6403) is:\n\n> \"For each mitigation plan created or revised in Part 2.3, implement the plan within the timeframe specified in the plan, unless a revision to the plan or an extension to the timeframe specified in Part 2.3 is approved by the CIP Senior Manager or delegate.\"\n\nThe deadline is **the timeframe the entity itself wrote into the plan**. The standard does not set an outer calendar deadline for Part 2.4 implementation. The Guidelines and Technical Basis confirm this explicitly (csection-ac05e06738e383a07698):\n\n> \"Remediation plans that have steps to be taken to remediate the vulnerability must be implemented by the timeframe the entity documented in their plan. **There is no maximum timeframe in this requirement** as patching and other system changes carries its own risk to the availability and integrity of the systems and may require waiting until a planned outage.\"\n\nSo the standard's structure is: Part 2.3 requires the plan to include \"a timeframe to complete these mitigations\" (and the GTB at csection-7d6ba196ae0e7c219624 notes timeframes \"can have event designations such as 'at next scheduled outage of at least two days duration'\"), and Part 2.4 then requires implementation by that self-set timeframe, with the CIP Senior Manager (or delegate) as the gate for any extension.\n\n## The operator's answer\n\nThe operator's procedure (LSPG-ADM-CIP007SPM v11.0, effective 2026-07-31) addresses this in Section 3.6 (isection-12bd999ecfa8bf61d440):\n\n- **3.6.2** requires mitigation plans to include \"a timeframe to complete any mitigations that are not in effect.\"\n- **3.6.4** requires SMEs to review plans each patch evaluation cycle and determine \"if the plan is still valid and is on schedule to be completed by the assigned mitigation date.\"\n- **3.6.5** escalates plans whose \"completion date is at risk\" to OT Security/EMS/Field Operations Management.\n- **3.6.7** assigns the CIP Senior Manager (or delegate) responsibility for approving any new or revised mitigation plan.\n\nThe policy (LSPG-POL-CIP003 v13.0, effective 2026-04-01) at Section 3.4.2.1 (isection-87d00aedd4cf1f41f0cd) restates the Part 2.4 duty verbatim: \"LSPG shall implement the plan within the timeframe specified in the plan, unless a revision to the plan or an extension to the timeframe specified is approved by the CIP Senior Manager (or Designee).\"\n\nThe CIP Senior Manager Process (isection-34eefd771edff96a7384, \u00a73.3.3) confirms the delegation: the CIP Senior Manager may delegate the Part 2.4 approval authority.\n\n## Does the operator set an outer deadline?\n\n**No.** The operator's procedure does not impose a maximum calendar deadline beyond the plan's own timeframe. It mirrors the standard's structure: the plan carries the date, the SME reviews it each cycle, at-risk plans are escalated, and the CIP Senior Manager (or delegate) approves extensions. There is no hardcoded \"must be done within X days\" figure in the operator's documents that I read.\n\nThe operator's procedure is, in this respect, a restatement of the standard's duty plus an operational review-and-escalation mechanism. It does not narrow the standard's latitude (which is \"no maximum\") to a fixed number, nor does it add one.\n\n## What I did not read\n\n- The `conflicts` component (3 sections) \u2014 I did not read it; if there is a recorded contradiction between the standard and an operator document on this Part, it would surface there. I found none in the four operator sections I did read.\n- The `vsl` component \u2014 not needed to answer the deadline question.\n- The `glossary`, `applicability`, `background`, `effective_dates`, `compliance_and_evidence_retention`, `version_history`, and `implementation_plan` components \u2014 not needed for this specific question.\n- The `csection-754b5967f6905d4c376e` (applicable systems) \u2014 the applicable systems are already stated in the requirement row I read.\n\nIf the analyst wants to confirm there is no recorded conflict on this Part, I would need to read the `conflicts` component.",
